StemStudio - vendored third-party inference code
=================================================

This directory contains source code from

  Music-Source-Separation-Training (MSST)
  https://github.com/ZFTurbo/Music-Source-Separation-Training
  Commit 1f700c386e0dd763fe0a57242bb9420dce987354
  Copyright (c) 2024 Roman Solovyev (ZFTurbo)
  Licensed under the MIT License (see LICENSE in this directory).

Files and modifications (each file carries a header naming its origin):

  attend.py              models/bs_roformer/attend.py, verbatim
  bs_roformer.py         models/bs_roformer/bs_roformer.py; beartype import and @beartype
                         decorators removed, Attend imported relatively
  mdx23c_tfc_tdf_v3.py   models/mdx23c_tfc_tdf_v3.py; prefer_target_instrument replaced by the
                         instrument count of the configuration
  configs.py             StemStudio file: hyper-parameters of config_drumsep_mdx23c.yaml and
                         mvsep_mega_model_bs_roformer_53_stems.yaml as Python constants (no
                         omegaconf / ml_collections), plus the two network builders

Training code, configuration loaders and GUI code of MSST are not included. The overlap-add
inference loop ("demix") is re-implemented in stemstudio_worker/detail/demix.py after
utils/model_utils.py of the same commit, accumulating only the instrument families StemStudio
uses.

The MDX-Net STFT wrapper for UVR MDX-Net KARA 2 (stemstudio_worker/detail/mdx_net.py) is
StemStudio code written after python-audio-separator (MIT License,
https://github.com/nomadkaraoke/python-audio-separator) and the Ultimate Vocal Remover project
(https://github.com/Anjok07/ultimatevocalremovergui). Credit: Ultimate Vocal Remover (UVR) and
its developers.

Model weights are not part of this directory or of the repository; they are downloaded at first
use (see stemstudio_worker/detail/registry.py and docs/decisions/ADR-009).
